config BR2_PACKAGE_OPENIPC_FAILSAFE
	bool "OpenIPC failsafe rescue + crash capture"
	help
	  Recovery machinery for SoC families whose U-Boot keeps a boot
	  counter in a reserved DRAM word and whose kernel reserves that
	  word and enables pstore/ramoops (currently Goke gk7205v200 and
	  gk7205v300).

	  Ships three pieces, none of which touch flash:

	    - failsafe-rescue: brings a camera up on network + SSH only,
	      skipping the SDK and streamer, when the bootloader has fallen
	      into failsafe after repeated failed boots;
	    - S99bootok: clears the DRAM boot counter once the image is
	      proven healthy, so a camera that boots but never streams still
	      escalates to failsafe instead of looping forever;
	    - S98crashlog: preserves the pstore crash log across a reboot for
	      the owner-pull crash report.

	  Enable it only on boards that reserve the counter; the address is
	  read from the board DTS, so on an image that does not reserve it
	  the counter writes are a safe no-op, but the scripts are dead
	  weight there and cost rootfs space.
